       M = 5.0:  J(0.02) = -2.261e-06 < 0,  J(40) = +1.456e+00 > 0,  L* = 5.38885   (sign changes on a 41-point log scan of (0.02, 40): 1; E* = L* H^2/e: any e is compatible with any L*)
  [PASS] Q4a sigma_HFY has no zero (Q3a) and the current has one sign change L*(M) at each of the four masses; L* is a field value, so it selects no coupling (existence of L* is descriptive; the coupling e is unconstrained because E is free)
     (c) massless conformal limit: the minimal scheme has (4/(3 pi)) ln M -> -infinity (no finite value); the maximal scheme has G_f^max(0) = -2/(9 pi) < 0, which no positive tie can match;
         with m = 0 the only scale besides H is the renormalization scale mu, and ln(mu/H) is a free input.
     note: L*(M) is not monotonic in M (descriptive).
     closed candidate list scored: 53 (six ties x four masses x two schemes, the M -> 0 maximal value, and L* at four masses); none selects a value of alpha.

